# .dockerignore — exkluderar build-artefakter, secrets, tests, frontend.
# Mindre build-context = snabbare docker build + mindre risk för accidental inkludering.

# .NET build-artefakter
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/TestResults/
**/coverage/
*.user
.vs/

# Tests — körs inte i image, bara i CI
tests/

# Frontend — bygger ur sin EGEN kontext (web/jobbliggaren-web/Dockerfile +
# dess egen .dockerignore), aldrig ur repo-roten.
web/

# Node
**/node_modules/
.next/
out/
.turbo/

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/

# Git
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/

# Dev secrets — must NEVER reach an image layer.
#
# THE `**/` FORMS ARE LOAD-BEARING, not style. A Docker pattern without a slash matches
# the context root only, and the Dockerfiles copy whole project directories
# (`COPY src/Jobbliggaren.Api/ src/Jobbliggaren.Api/`). Measured 2026-08-05 against a
# build-context probe using this file: under the old root-anchored form both
# `src/Jobbliggaren.Api/appsettings.Local.json` and a nested `*.pem` reached the context,
# as did `deploy/.env` — the file the runbook tells the operator to create with the master
# key and all four database passwords. The main checkout carries a real Local.json, and the
# Web SDK's default glob pulls in `appsettings.*.json` without any csproj listing them,
# proven on the artefact. CI is clean only because these are gitignored; a local
# `docker build` is not, and #196 publishes these images publicly.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/appsettings.Local.json
**/.secrets/
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# Terraform — separat lifecycle
infra/

# Docs — onödigt i image
docs/
*.md
!**/README.md

# Claude Code
.claude/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Logs
*.log
logs/

# Husky — finns inte i image
.husky/
